### 10.1 Required Demo Scenarios

1. Compare static routing with hysteresis-enabled self-healing after a forwarding node is terminated.
2. Compare hysteresis-enabled recovery against naïve threshold recovery; show route flap count difference.
3. Transfer a file over multiple paths with DB-DSP; interrupt one path; verify final SHA-256.
4. Compare DB-DSP, round-robin, weighted round-robin, naïve delay-aware, and single-path on the same heterogeneous topology; present the comparison table.
5. Compare RTX-CL vs. RTX-CWND under mixed loss conditions; present transfer time difference.
6. Run repeated benchmarks under `tc`/`netem`-controlled delay, loss, and rate limits; export results.
7. Attempt an unauthorised route change and replay an old heartbeat; show rejection and audit records.
8. Stop PostgreSQL during a run and demonstrate the documented forwarding behaviour.

