## 13. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Scope creep | Three features only. Keep feature-specific MVPs and acceptance tests. |
| Hysteresis parameters hard to tune | Make configurable; sweep as an experimental variable. |
| DB-DSP estimates noisy | EWMA smoothing; document estimator and limitations. |
| RTX-CL depends on accurate `cwnd` estimate | Document estimation method; validate against known loss scenarios. |
| `tc`/`netem` requires elevated privileges | Document setup; run node processes as non-root where possible; use `sudo` for `tc` configuration only. |
| Emulation is not real networking | Document clearly; label synthetic conditions; validate emulator against configured values. |
| `tc`/`netem` kernel version differences | Record kernel version in every run; document any known behaviour changes. |
| Dashboard hides missing behaviour | Prove CLI/end-to-end flows before building polished UI. |
| Routing loops or stale state | Versioned routes, hop limits, next-hop validation, loop tests. |
| Misleading packet-loss metric | Distinguish app-message loss from datagram loss; document TCP retransmission effects. |
| Multipath performs worse | Compare to single-path baseline; document cases with no improvement. |
| Security only exists on paper | Automated negative tests and visible rejection events. |
| PostgreSQL becomes bottleneck | Batch writes; keep DB off the forwarding hot path. |
| Docker resource overhead | Keep node processes native by default; containerise only infrastructure. |
| Noisy laptop measurements | Record environment, repeat tests, avoid overclaiming generalisation. |

